From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:13:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Find the station by link address in the association TX status

A non-AP MLD station is stored under its MLD MAC address. If the driver
did not translate the source address of the (Re)Association Request
frame to the MLD MAC address, handle_assoc() addresses the response to
the link address, and the TX status carries that address too.
handle_assoc_cb() then does not find the station, the association is
never completed, and the peer waits for an EAPOL-Key frame that is never
sent.

Also look up the station by its link address, as handle_auth_cb() does.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -10274,6 +10274,12 @@
 	bool epp_sta = false;
 
 	sta = ap_get_sta(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	/* A non-AP MLD is registered under its MLD MAC address, while the
+	 * response was addressed to the link address it associated from. */
+	if (!sta)
+		sta = ap_get_link_sta(hapd, mgmt->da);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	if (!sta) {
 		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "handle_assoc_cb: STA " MACSTR " not found",
 			   MAC2STR(mgmt->da));
